# Cursor Model Pin

When calling `Task` or launching subagents, **always** set `model` to `cursor-grok-4.5-high`.

Do **not**:

- Omit `model` on `Task` launches (soft rule — Phase B still allows omit so the High parent can inherit)
- Pass `inherit`, `cursor-grok-4.5-fast`, `cursor-grok-4.5`, `composer-*`, Claude, GPT, Terra, or Sol slugs
- Rely on Explore’s faster default — operators SHOULD set CLI `exploreSubagentModel: "inherit"` in user-owned `~/.cursor/cli-config.json` (sync SHALL NOT write `cli-config` or live `state.vscdb`)

Custom agents under `.cursor/agents/` (and managed home agents) are pinned to `cursor-grok-4.5-high`.

## Layer matrix (SSOT)

| Layer | Mechanism | Omit `model` | Wrong/fast model | Hook crash |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Soft rule | `.cursor/rules/cursor-models.mdc` | Agents must not omit | Agents must not pass | N/A |
| Phase A | `preToolUse` Task rewrite | Pins to High via `updated_input` | Rewrites + clears alts | **fail-open** (Task proceeds) |
| Phase B | `subagentStart` allowlist | Allow (inherit High parent) | Deny if explicit non-High | **fail-open** |
| Validate/CI | `validate_hooks` + pytest | N/A | N/A | Compensatory: projection **must** exist |

Security Enforce guards (`beforeShellExecution`, etc.) stay **fail-closed** (RV-004). Pin hooks stay **fail-open**.
